  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "processBinaryMessage",
    "file": "open62541/src/server/ua_server_binary.c",
    "description": "processBinaryMessage unconditionally calls UA_Connection_sendError(connection, ...) when UA_Connection_processChunks returns an error. But UA_Connection_processChunks may already have triggered connection teardown/free of the underlying send buffer via deeper processing (e.g., MSG handling path through processMSG -> UA_deleteMembers on data tied to the connection buffer). The code then reuses connection state/buffer pointers during error encoding, leading to a heap-use-after-free in UInt32_encodeBinary while writing the ERR header.",
    "conditions": "In fuzz_binary_message, a crafted binary packet sequence causes chunk processing to fail after a path that frees memory backing the connection send buffer (allocated in createDummyConnection). processBinaryMessage receives non-GOOD retval and attempts to send an ERR response on the same connection. Because the relevant buffer/state was already freed during prior processing, UA_Connection_sendError encodes into freed memory, producing UAF. Trigger requires malformed chunk/message flow that both induces an internal processing error and causes prior cleanup/free before the error-response send."
  },
